{"word": "criterion", "source": "freedictionaryapi", "data": {"word": "criterion", "entries": [{"language": {"code": "en", "name": "English"}, "partOfSpeech": "noun", "pronunciations": [{"type": "ipa", "text": "/kɹɪˈtɪəɹi.ən/", "tags": []}, {"type": "ipa", "text": "/kɹaɪˈtɪə.ɹi.ən/", "tags": ["Received Pronunciation"]}, {"type": "ipa", "text": "/kɹaɪˈtɪɹ.i.ən/", "tags": ["General American"]}], "forms": [{"word": "criteria", "tags": ["plural"]}, {"word": "criterions", "tags": ["plural", "rare"]}, {"word": "criteria", "tags": ["alternative"]}, {"word": "criterium", "tags": ["alternative"]}], "senses": [{"definition": "A standard, test, or requirement by which individual things or people may be compared and judged; a gauge.", "tags": [], "examples": ["Near-synonym: benchmark", "criterion of choice, of decision, of selection"], "quotes": [{"text": "Knowledge has come to her too soon—knowledge of evil, unqualified by the general charities which longer experience infallibly brings; but her age has lent its own freshness to this first great emotion; it becomes unconsciously a criterion, and the judgment is harsh, because the remembrance is bitter.", "reference": "1834, L[etitia] E[lizabeth] L[andon], chapter XXVII, in Francesca Carrara. […], volume I, London: Richard Bentley, […], (successor to Henry Colburn), →OCLC, page 310:"}, {"text": "The Enlightment worldview, which considered the order of \"Nature\" as a basis and, at the same time, the subject of explorations of scientific natural sciences, has, at the same time, considered this order as a criterion of the artistically-aesthetic qualities of art. From an \"ideological\" point of view, it liberated art from its feudal religious and courtly servitude.", "reference": "1986, Piotr Buczkowski, Andrzej Klawiter, editors, Theories of Ideology and Ideology of Theories, Rodopi, →ISBN, →ISSN, page 57:"}, {"text": "Congratulations on managing to use the phrase “preponderant criterion” in a chart (“On your marks”, November 9th). Was this the work of a kakorrhaphiophobic journalist set a challenge by his colleagues, or simply an example of glossolalia?", "reference": "2013 November 30, Paul Davis, “Letters: Say it as simply as possible”, in The Economist, volume 409, number 8864:"}], "synonyms": ["benchmark"], "antonyms": [], "translations": [{"language": {"code": "sq", "name": "Albanian"}, "word": "kriter"}, {"language": {"code": "ar", "name": "Arabic"}, "word": "مِعْيَار"}, {"language": {"code": "hy", "name": "Armenian"}, "word": "չափանիշ"}, {"language": {"code": "ast", "name": "Asturian"}, "word": "criteriu"}, {"language": {"code": "az", "name": "Azerbaijani"}, "word": "meyar"}, {"language": {"code": "az", "name": "Azerbaijani"}, "word": "mizan"}, {"language": {"code": "az", "name": "Azerbaijani"}, "word": "kriteri"}, {"language": {"code": "be", "name": "Belarusian"}, "word": "крытэ́рый"}, {"language": {"code": "be", "name": "Belarusian"}, "word": "ме́рыва"}, {"language": {"code": "be", "name": "Belarusian"}, "word": "ме́рка"}, {"language": {"code": "bg", "name": "Bulgarian"}, "word": "крите́рий"}, {"language": {"code": "bg", "name": "Bulgarian"}, "word": "мери́ло"}, {"language": {"code": "ca", "name": "Catalan"}, "word": "criteri"}, {"language": {"code": "cmn", "name": "Chinese Mandarin"}, "word": "標準 /标准"}, {"language": {"code": "cmn", "name": "Chinese Mandarin"}, "word": "尺度"}, {"language": {"code": "cmn", "name": "Chinese Mandarin"}, "word": "準則 /准则"}, {"language": {"code": "cmn", "name": "Chinese Mandarin"}, "word": "軌範 /轨范"}, {"language": {"code": "cs", "name": "Czech"}, "word": "kritérium"}, {"language": {"code": "cs", "name": "Czech"}, "word": "kriterium"}, {"language": {"code": "da", "name": "Danish"}, "word": "kriterium"}, {"language": {"code": "nl", "name": "Dutch"}, "word": "criterium"}, {"language": {"code": "eo", "name": "Esperanto"}, "word": "kriterio"}, {"language": {"code": "et", "name": "Estonian"}, "word": "kriteerium"}, {"language": {"code": "fi", "name": "Finnish"}